> (which I haven't found yet.) I have a large stack of spellbooks, a
> couple of which are blessed, and I could bless the rest if I tried.
> Would it be worth even trying to be a spellcaster?

Yeah.  My preferred configuration for valks is GDSM + amulet of
reflection, or (if possible) MR-granting artifact and SDSM.  Either
setup leaves the cloak slot free for a robe; with a robe, you can
become a decent caster.  As a neutral, I'll avoid generating any
artifacts if possible until wishing for the Eye; that gives mana
regen, branchport, and MR and leaves the amulet slot open for "oLS or
the Eye itself ("oESP).  But I'd generally prefer "oReflection + GDSM
+ robe over SDSM + CoMR + "oLS.

Adding a helm of brilliance (and boosting stats with gain ability, !
oEnlightenment, etc) helps too, but you don't need to be completely
maxed to get reasonable results.

> And how should I protect my stash? Is a locked chest on a square with
> Elbereth burned on the floor good enough? Should I surround it with
> boulders and levitate in and out? How far do you go to protect it?

The former is good enough unless you have strong pets.  I tend to use
a sack rather than a chest unless there's a chest generated
conveniently (since I prefer the first level of sokoban for my stash,
that's uncommon...)



